Gives each exec ctx of the Stellux nvkmd an overflow list, so a submit
never waits for room in a full queue. Such a wait would hang a program
whose queued work depends on a point its own thread signals after the
submit. The list takes the submission the full queue refuses and every
later one while the list holds any, and the ctx's thread submits them in
order as the queue drains, waking at least every 100 ms for the device
check. A submit fails with VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_HOST_MEMORY when its submission
cannot be copied onto the list or the thread cannot start. A loss drops
the list, whose submissions never reach the kernel. A ctx's sync waits for
the list to empty, and its destroy stops its thread. Making or destroying
a ctx waits for the dev's other threads to leave their lists before it
changes the dev's list of ctxs, which their device checks walk.

